# The authority that published this deployment's ladder presets. Without it
# the app labels every config as third-party and never offers to create one.
# `bun run configs:init` prints the value to use.
VITE_TAPER_ADMIN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RPC endpoints
#
# Each public network has two slots, because the endpoint you hand to every
# visitor and the endpoint you pay for by the request are rarely the same URL.
# Paste into both and nothing else needs configuring; leave one blank and it
# falls back as described under it.
#
# Pool and position browsing is `getProgramAccounts`, which the public
# endpoints rate-limit per IP — a busy page hits 429 part way through a list
# and looks broken — and which some providers refuse outright. So neither slot
# wants a default endpoint if you can help it.
#
# A visitor can always point their own browser at their own endpoint from the
# RPC chip in the header. That is stored in their `localStorage`, needs no
# rebuild, and is why neither slot is a hard requirement.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- what a BUILD ships with -----------------------------------------------
# Inlined into the JS bundle every visitor downloads, so it is public to
# anyone who opens the app: a paid endpoint here is a shared quota with a key
# you can only revoke by rotating. These are the names to set in the Vercel
# project rather than in a committed file.
#
# A production build has no dev server in front of it, so check that whatever
# goes here answers OPTIONS with `access-control-allow-origin` before shipping
# it — an endpoint that mishandles the CORS preflight makes the deployed page
# read as offline while working perfectly under `bun run dev`.
#
# Mainnet is hidden from the network picker until VITE_MAINNET_RPC is set.
# That is not a guard — the program has the same address everywhere and anyone
# may point a browser at it — it is because the public mainnet endpoint
# refuses this app's getProgramAccounts, so offering mainnet without an
# endpoint offers a page that cannot list a pool.
VITE_MAINNET_RPC=
VITE_DEVNET_RPC=

# --- what THIS MACHINE uses -------------------------------------------------
# Wins over the slot above whenever the dev server is running, and is ignored
# by a production build. `bun run dev` proxies it through the Vite server
# (`/rpc/devnet`, `/rpc/mainnet`) instead of letting the page call it
# cross-origin, so the key never enters the dev bundle and an endpoint that
# mishandles the CORS preflight still works locally.
#
# `bun run configs:init` and the deploy script read these two first
# as well, so a paid endpoint pasted here is used by everything that talks to a
# public cluster from this machine, with no --url flag to remember.
#
# Blank means "use the build slot above"; both blank means the SDK's public
# default.
VITE_MAINNET_RPC_DEV=
VITE_DEVNET_RPC_DEV=

# --- localnet ---------------------------------------------------------------
# `scripts/start-localnet.ps1`. One slot: it is local by definition, never
# bundled anywhere it could be reached, and has no WebSocket.
VITE_LOCALNET_RPC=http://127.0.0.1:8899
